# Every image the published wiki carries, one per line, sorted.
#
# The wiki markdown lives in this repo; the images live in the wiki
# repository (github.com/fdittgen-png/tankstellen.wiki.git) because they
# are large binaries with their own history. That split used to make the
# 'an image a page references exists' guard a no-op: it bailed out when the
# image folders were absent, which in this repo is ALWAYS (#4044).
#
# This manifest is the hermetic stand-in. Regenerate it whenever images are
# added, removed or renamed, in the same commit as the markdown that points
# at them:
#
#   dart run tool/wiki_image_manifest.dart --write
#
# guide/_tooling/ is deliberately excluded: it holds the capture-pipeline
# state (manifest.json, README.txt), not page images.
